  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe aim to improve the upper bound for the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem constant C\u2085 by finding a step function h that minimizes the maximum overlap integral. The previous approach used a discretized h and optimization with SLSQP and gradient descent. Here, we propose a multi-resolution optimization approach that begins with a coarse discretization, progressively increasing it while leveraging solutions from lower resolutions as initial guesses for higher ones. This strategy balances exploration with exploitation, starting from a broader search space before refining the solution.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n- Variables: h: [0, 2] \u2192 [0, 1], discretized into n_points intervals.\n- Objective: Minimize C\u2085 = max_k [\u222b h(x)(1 - h(x + k)) dx]\n- Constraints: \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x) dx = 1; 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x.\n- The overlap integral is computed via cross-correlation, ensuring non-circular convolution with appropriate boundary handling.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\nInitialization:\na. Start with a low resolution (n_points = 10) and gradually increase.\nb. If initial_h_values are available, use them as a seed.\n\nOptimization loop:\n1. For each resolution level (from low to high):\n   a. Up-sample the solution from the previous resolution.\n   b. Use a combination of global and local search:\n      i. Initial phase: Differential Evolution for global exploration.\n      ii. Refinement phase: SLSQP for local optimization.\n   c. After each iteration, project h back into feasible region:\n      - Clip values to [0, 1]\n      - Adjust to ensure sum(h) = n_points / 2\n   d. Compute current C\u2085 and track improvements.\n   e. If improvement stalls, perturb h slightly and restart.\n\nTermination:\n- Stop when budget_s is exhausted or C\u2085 \u2264 0.3807 is achieved.\n- Return the best h found along with its C\u2085 value.\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Start with n_points =10, doubling each step up to 200.\n- Use a population size of 20 for Differential Evolution.\n- Set SLSQP's maxiter to 200 for refinement.\n- Perturbation step of 0.01 when stalling detected.\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Each resolution level takes ~10% of total budget.\n- Monitor wall-clock time within each optimization phase.\n- Maintain a feasible fallback candidate at all times.\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Ensure h is within [0, 1] and sum to n_points/2.\n- Validate C\u2085 computation matches task metric.\n- Return (h, C\u2085, n_points) as per function signature.",
